+# Production menu adoption of the Blender UI atlas
+
+Baseline: `f4e8ad98efe20c2e68643570b4ee007f93e0f780`, private branch
+`codex/ui-atlas-game-adoption`. This slice adopts the already reviewed frozen
+atlas; it does not regenerate or extend the art.
+
+## Production changes
+
+`src/ui/screens/menu.js` explicitly adopts four navigation controls: Career,
+iMarket, Garage and Settings. Each keeps its existing DOM button, icon, live
+label, tap handler and destination. The graphics-quality preference adopts four
+compact controls, with mutually exclusive `aria-pressed` state and an underline
+on the selected label. Switches and audio sliders retain their existing behavior.
+
+The main Play action retains its existing full-width, 56px layout. Its full
+`Play`, `Continue` and `Resume Hole` labels remain in the DOM, and its accessible
+name now follows the visible label. There is no global Button replacement.
+
+`src/ui/screens/menu-atlas.css` supplies menu-only grid slots. A slot exposes the
+available width to the consumer; a face that cannot fit uses the readable flat
+fallback. Quality controls use two rows. Authored spacing is UI design, not a
+physical machine specification (`NOT SOURCED`).
+
+## Reusable opt-in contract
+
+```js
+import { mountBlenderAtlas } from './blender-atlas.js';
+
+// Attach root first. Each opted-in native button has exactly one direct label
+// wrapper containing both its existing icon and live label.
+button.dataset.buiButton = 'neutral'; // or 'accent'
+button.dataset.buiSize = 'standard'; // or 'compact'
+// <button ...><span class="bui-button__label">...</span></button>
+const atlas = mountBlenderAtlas(root);
+await atlas.ready; // true only after validation and selected image decode
+// false leaves a readable fallback. refresh() is an explicit failure retry.
+await atlas.refresh();
+atlas.dispose();
+```
+
+The module imports the existing Blender motion stylesheet and scoped atlas
+stylesheet. Native dimensions, safe regions, foregrounds and sprite coordinates
+are read from the manifest. Production selectors override existing button
+surface/press scaling only for explicit `data-bui-button` controls. State styles
+cover native disabled, existing tap classes, pointer active, selected and focus.
+Both the OS motion preference and the shell's live reduced-motion class apply.
+
+The default deployment base is Vite's `BASE_URL`, resolved against the document
+base URI. The optional `baseUrl` is the **deployment directory**, not the atlas
+directory; the consumer appends `ui/blender/`. Successful manifests are shared
+by absolute URL, and decoded images by URL and expected dimensions. Failures
+are evicted so an explicit refresh/remount can retry. Shared in-flight requests
+are bounded by a ten-second operational timeout, and are not cancelled by the
+departure of one consumer while another may still need them.
+
+Text fitting measures live glyph bounds, the combined icon/label wrapper,
+scroll bounds and the available parent width. Oversized labels, enlarged text,
+invalid label markup and unavailable assets use a wrapping DOM fallback. No
+face is stretched, cropped, or reduced below the authored native target. Font
+completion, relevant label/style mutations, resize and display-density changes
+schedule remeasurement. Unrelated player statistics do not schedule a refit.
+
+Mounting the same root again returns its existing controller. Disposal cancels
+the controller's queued frame and disconnects its observers and font/resize/DPR
+listeners; late shared completion cannot mutate a disposed root. Menu unmount
+and sheet close use `dispose({preserveAppearance:true})`: the final decoration
+stays visible through the shell's existing dismissal animation while runtime
+work stops. A weak ownership snapshot permits later remount and complete
+restoration. Menu `destroy()` also disposes open settings controllers when the
+shell itself is torn down.
+
+## Verification and integration boundary
+
+- `node tools/check-blender-atlas-consumer.mjs`: 22 CPU cases pass. Geometry in
+  these cases is synthetic; this result is not rendered-layout evidence.
+- `node tools/check-ui-atlas.mjs --self-test`: frozen atlas gate passes; eleven
+  intentionally corrupt fixtures are rejected.
+- `node tools/ui-atlas-adoption-review/serve.mjs --build`: actual menu/shell
+  harness builds. It instantiates the production UI, components and content,
+  with no renderer, simulation or model loader instance.
+- An independent HTTP check of the built `/menu-review/` subpath matched all
+  35 public atlas/manifest files byte for byte and served its compiled entry
+  JavaScript and CSS. Report: `shots/ui-atlas-adoption/build-http.json`.
+- Headed review and its source hashes are recorded separately in
+  `research/ui-atlas-adoption-review.md` when complete. GPU ownership must
+  explicitly name `ui-atlas-adoption` before that harness runs.
+
+Root owns package and production build wiring. No build configuration change is
+needed to load this opt-in consumer: `menu.js` imports it, it imports its CSS,
+and the existing public-asset emitter already emits `public/ui/blender/**`.
+Recommended CPU gate addition is `node tools/check-blender-atlas-consumer.mjs`;
+retain the existing atlas export gate. No package script was edited here.
+
+The private worktree has no game models. Root must run the actual-game smoke
+against its served integration checkout after applying/reviewing the patch:
+
+```powershell
+node tools/check-ui-atlas-game-smoke.mjs --url http://127.0.0.1:5178/ --lease root-integration --out shots/ui-atlas-game-smoke
+```
+
+Replace the URL and lease with the actual served base and explicitly granted
+owner. The smoke verifies the active rig's actual `glb:` source, live context,
+production atlas responses, menu/settings faces, preferences and navigation.
+The task root has syntax-checked this script; a full-game result is pending root
+integration. Root also retains the complete build/artifact check. Neither the
+isolated DOM evidence nor this menu smoke establishes FPS, an AAA verdict or a
+general accessibility verdict.
