+# Actual menu atlas adoption review
+
+Review workspace: `drillity-ui-atlas-game-adoption`, baseline `f4e8ad9`.
+
+The isolated harness imports the production `createUI` shell, which imports the
+actual `createMenuScreen`, components, styles, and other screen factories. State
+and catalogue content come from `createGameState`, `createBus`, and `game/data.js`.
+No renderer, simulation or GLB loader is instantiated. This can establish menu
+DOM integration and lifecycle behavior; it cannot establish whole-game render
+quality, FPS, a general accessibility pass, or an AAA verdict.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+The existing dependency junction is read only. No packages are installed and no
+package/build wiring is modified. Port 5201 must be free. The headed checker
+refuses to launch unless the shared `gpu-owner.txt` exactly names
+`ui-atlas-adoption`; obtain the parent task's explicit delegation as well.
+
+```powershell
+node tools/ui-atlas-adoption-review/serve.mjs --build
+node tools/ui-atlas-adoption-review/serve.mjs --preview
+node tools/ui-atlas-adoption-review/check.mjs
+```
+
+The production harness is served under `/menu-review/`. Its isolated output
+copies only the atlas public directory, not game models. The full shell also
+causes the existing dynamically imported tooling code to be emitted; it is not
+executed by these menu checks. The page uses the production Google Fonts link;
+the report records whether Inter is available during each measurement.
+
+## Current evidence status
+
+CPU syntax checks and the isolated Vite production build pass. The initial
+harness used a top-level await incompatible with Vite's default targets; moving
+its startup into an async function fixed that harness issue. No production
+target setting was changed.
+
+Headed execution remains pending an explicit GPU lease. Prepared cases cover
+320/390/430 CSS pixels, 1x/2x density, measured 200% text enlargement, full dynamic
+Play labels, keyboard and pointer behavior, native target and safe-region
+geometry, missing/corrupt/delayed assets and explicit recovery, live density and
+font/parent-size changes, repeated mounts, settings disposal and shell disposal
+while loading. The text fixture doubles the actual computed typography tokens
+and adopted control sizes; it is not a full-page zoom test.
+
+The report will be written to
+`tools/ui-atlas-adoption-review/evidence/report.json`, together with screenshots
+and SHA-256 source hashes. Existing atlas authoring evidence is untouched.
+
+Source review of the parent's actual-game smoke found one fixture assumption:
+the reduced-motion check blindly toggled an existing saved preference. The
+parent made that operation conditional on its current checked state. The smoke
+requires the full integration checkout and matching GLBs and is not executed
+from this private harness.
